   "title": "Romanian demonstratives: acest, acel and their friends",
   "summary": "Romanian has two degrees of distance, acest (this) and acel (that), which agree with the noun in gender, number and case. They can stand before a bare noun (acest copil) or after a noun with the definite article (copilul acesta), and everyday speech has short colloquial forms (ăsta, ăla).",
